  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAK023N Pakistan DRA Flood Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Subtitle" promeva:type="3" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRA Flood Response</narrative>
  </description>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pakistan DRA Flood Response proposes a multi-sectoral response in 13 districts in the 4 main provinces. The regions were selected as first priority locations, based on the severity of the flood situation, number of affected people, and IPC level (areas facing IPC 3 and above). The objective of the JR is to provide 92.646 flood-affected people with lifesaving humanitarian assistance. The partners have designed their response based on needs and gaps, their technical expertise and complementarity with other interventions to maximise impact. Selected activities are in line with humanitarian and cluster recommendations/standards. The response is a multi-sector approach with Food Security and Livelihoods (FSL), Health, Shelter/NFI, MPC and WASH interventions with Protection being mainstreamed.</narrative>
  </description>
